+
+# Best AI Tools for Interior Designers in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-interior-designers-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for interior designers in 2026 are increasingly open source, local-first, and GitHub-native. This list focuses only on public GitHub repositories that help with room concept renders, inpainting, object removal, segmentation, depth estimation, and 3D reconstruction workflows relevant to interior design teams.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `ComfyUI`, `InvokeAI`, and `AUTOMATIC1111/stable-diffusion-webui` are the strongest open-source starting points for local concept rendering and iterative room visualization.
+- `IOPaint`, `ControlNet`, and `Real-ESRGAN` are especially useful for fast staging edits, reference-guided redesigns, and presentation-quality cleanup.
+- `Segment Anything`, `GroundingDINO`, and `Depth Anything V2` are the best picks when you need masks, object localization, and depth maps for redesign pipelines.
+- `nerfstudio`, `Open3D`, `DUSt3R`, and `gaussian-splatting` are the most relevant repos for turning photos of real spaces into navigable 3D assets.
+- Dedicated open-source AI repos specifically for floor plans and interior layout generation remain a real gap; most strong tooling still sits in broader vision and 3D ecosystems.
+
+## Why This List
+Open-source AI matters for interior design because teams often need privacy, local control, custom style tuning, and reproducible design workflows. Instead of pointing to closed SaaS products, this list tracks public GitHub repositories that interior designers can inspect, self-host, fine-tune, extend, and combine into their own rendering, renovation-visualization, and space-analysis stacks.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Image Generation, Inpainting, and Enhancement
+
+#### [ComfyUI](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI)
+> **Description:** ComfyUI describes itself as a modular visual AI engine built around graph and node workflows for Stable Diffusion pipelines. For interior designers, that matters because room styling, material swaps, lighting studies, and variant generation often benefit from reusable node graphs instead of one-off prompts. Its README emphasizes local execution, cross-platform support, and sharable workflows, which makes it strong for repeatable design explorations and team templates. GitHub shows very active maintenance and large community adoption: last commit `2026-03-26`, `108k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `GPL-3.0`.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI)
