+> **Description:** Segment Anything is a foundation segmentation model that produces masks from prompts such as points or boxes and can also generate masks across an entire image. For interior design workflows, that is useful when isolating walls, rugs, sofas, cabinets, lighting fixtures, or windows before editing or measuring. The README emphasizes strong zero-shot segmentation and easy inference, which makes it a common building block in room redesign tooling. GitHub metadata from the repo shows last commit `2024-09-18`, `53.8k` stars, primary language `Jupyter Notebook`, license `Apache-2.0`.
