+## TL;DR
+- `ComfyUI`, `InvokeAI`, and `AUTOMATIC1111/stable-diffusion-webui` are the strongest open-source starting points for local concept rendering and iterative room visualization.
+- `IOPaint`, `ControlNet`, and `Real-ESRGAN` are especially useful for fast staging edits, reference-guided redesigns, and presentation-quality cleanup.
+- `Segment Anything`, `GroundingDINO`, and `Depth Anything V2` are the best picks when you need masks, object localization, and depth maps for redesign pipelines.
+- `nerfstudio`, `Open3D`, `DUSt3R`, and `gaussian-splatting` are the most relevant repos for turning photos of real spaces into navigable 3D assets.
+- Dedicated open-source AI repos specifically for floor plans and interior layout generation remain a real gap; most strong tooling still sits in broader vision and 3D ecosystems.
+
+## Why This List
+Open-source AI matters for interior design because teams often need privacy, local control, custom style tuning, and reproducible design workflows. Instead of pointing to closed SaaS products, this list tracks public GitHub repositories that interior designers can inspect, self-host, fine-tune, extend, and combine into their own rendering, renovation-visualization, and space-analysis stacks.
