+### Floor Plans and Layout Automation
+
+Dedicated open-source GitHub repos specifically for AI-powered interior floor planning and furniture layout were a verified gap during research. I found plenty of strong open repos for rendering, masking, depth, and 3D reconstruction, but fewer than 5 clearly maintained public GitHub repos that were both interior-layout-specific and strong enough to recommend here without stretching the theme.
+
+If you contribute to this repo, this is the category with the clearest opportunity: public GitHub repos for room-layout optimization, floor-plan parsing, furniture arrangement, or code-first space planning.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open-source AI tools for interior designers in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting stack is `ComfyUI` or `InvokeAI` for generation, `IOPaint` for cleanup, `ControlNet` for layout-preserving edits, `Segment Anything` for masking, and `nerfstudio` or `Open3D` for 3D capture workflows.
+
+### Are there any free AI interior design tools on GitHub that are not SaaS?
+Yes. Every project in this list is a public GitHub repository. Many can run locally or self-hosted, which is the main reason they were included.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for redesigning a room from an existing photo?
+Start with `IOPaint`, `ControlNet`, `Segment Anything`, `Grounded-Segment-Anything`, and `ComfyUI`. That combination covers object removal, structure-preserving generation, masking, and pipeline orchestration.
+
+### What open-source AI repos help turn room photos into 3D scenes?
+`nerfstudio`, `gaussian-splatting`, `DUSt3R`, `Open3D`, and `PyTorch3D` are the most relevant repos here. They serve different levels of the pipeline, from reconstruction to geometry processing.
+
+### Are there open-source GitHub alternatives to proprietary AI room-staging tools?
+Yes, but they are more composable than all-in-one. A practical alternative stack is `ComfyUI` or `InvokeAI` plus `IOPaint`, `ControlNet`, and `Real-ESRGAN`.
+
+### Which repos are best for building a custom interior design AI workflow?
+If you want code-level flexibility, use `diffusers`, `MMagic`, `MMSegmentation`, `MMDetection`, `PyTorch3D`, and `Open3D`. Those are better foundations for internal tooling than click-first apps.
+
+### Why are there so few floor-plan-specific open-source AI repos in this list?
+Because the open-source market is still stronger in rendering and computer vision than in furniture-layout optimization. Rather than padding the list with weak matches, this repo calls out that gap directly.
+
